# TELCO CUSTOMER CHURN ANALYSIS

## Overview

This project explores the IBM Telco Customer Churn dataset to identify the factors that influence customer churn and provide insights that can help improve customer retention.

An interactive Power BI dashboard was developed to analyze customer demographics, subscribed services, contract types, and billing information.

---

## Dataset

* Source: IBM Telco Customer Churn Dataset
* Total Records: 7,043 customers
* Total Features: 21 columns

The dataset includes:

* Customer demographics
* Services subscribed
* Contract details
* Billing information
* Customer tenure
* Churn status

---

## Dashboard Pages

### Overview

* Total Customers
* Active Customers
* Churn Rate
* Average Monthly Charges
* Churn by Contract Type

## Services Analysis

* Internet Service
* Online Security
* Tech Support
* Fiber Optic Customer Analysis

## Demographic Analysis

* Gender
* Partner Status
* Customer Tenure
* Senior Citizen Analysis

---

## Key Insights

* Overall churn rate is 26.54%, meaning more than 1 out of every 4 customers left the company.
* Customers on month-to-month contracts recorded the highest churn rate.
* Churned customers had a higher average monthly charge ($74.44) than retained customers ($61.27).
* Customers using Fiber Optic Internet were more likely to churn.
* Customers without Online Security and Tech Support services had a higher tendency to leave.
* Female customers accounted for a slightly larger share of churn cases.
* Customers without partners were more likely to churn.
* Customers with 0–12 months tenure represented the largest share of churn.

---

## Recommendations

* Encourage customers to switch to long-term contracts.
* Review pricing strategies for high-paying customers.
* Promote value-added services such as Online Security and Tech Support.
* Focus retention efforts on new customers.
* Develop targeted campaigns for high-risk customer segments.

